goal:
An ON SELECT rule has to be named _RETURN and a rule of any other kind has to not be. Creating a rule enforces this, and a good deal of client code relies on it. Renaming one does not: a non-SELECT rule can be renamed to _RETURN.

The result cannot be dumped and restored, because the CREATE RULE command the dump produces is rejected on the way back in.

    CREATE RULE r AS ON INSERT TO t DO INSTEAD NOTHING;
    ALTER RULE r ON t RENAME TO "_RETURN";

The rename has to be refused. Renaming an ON SELECT rule to _RETURN, and renames not involving that name at all, must keep working.
